Perfect! I have completed my research and compiled the final results. Let me provide you with the summary:

## Research Summary

I conducted extensive research across 7 different question angles (full AI IDEs, CLIs/terminal agents, workflow-specific tools, project memory tools, open-source agents, IDE integrations, and workflow orchestration agents) to find newly launched AI coding tools in the last 14 days (April 16-30, 2026).

### Findings

After thorough investigation across multiple sources including:
- Web searches for product launches
- Google I/O 2026 announcements
- GitHub repositories and trending
- Product Hunt and developer communities
- Wikipedia entries for new products

### Result

**Only one confirmed new product launch** was found within the 14-day window:

**Google Antigravity** (Launched: April 16, 2026)
- A full AI IDE positioning itself as a direct competitor to Cursor and Windsurf
- Agent-first approach with multi-agent coordination system
- Features R.A.P.S Framework for parallel agent management
- Deep integration with Google Cloud and built-in Chrome for testing
- Featured prominently at Google I/O 2026 as part of the "agentic era"

### Notable Exclusions

Several products were investigated but **excluded** because they were either:
- **Model updates** to existing products (e.g., Claude Opus 4.7, Claude Sonnet 5, Gemma 4)
- **Launched prior to April 16, 2026** (e.g., Claude Code CLI in May 2025, DeepSeek Coder V3 in January 2026)
- **Outside the scope** (not AI coding/developer tools)

The final results have been written to `new-product.json` in the specified directory.

